  "rewrites": {
   "4": {
    "original": "The likes of Ireland, Scotland and Wales won\u2019t mind too much having to go through pot one as these nations benefit from the so-called fair draw concept - you\u2019re fixed in a group consisting of small clubs, well tutored, and then you can crash through qualifying in four two-legged encounters.",
    "rewrite": "Nations such as Ireland, Scotland, and Wales aren't likely to object to staying in pot one because they gain advantage from the fair draw system\u2014ending up in a group with lesser-known clubs, well-prepared teams, and progressing by outmaneuvering four smaller opponents in two-match series."
   },
   "15": {
    "original": "Up until now FFA - one of only two associations which publicly and loudly opposed the move - had advocated an 80-team tournament with the top 24 nations in the world and platoons of qualifiers from the non-elite nations.",
    "rewrite": "Up until this point, FFA\u2014one of the lone two associations to publicly oppose the change\u2014had advocated for an 80-team tournament featuring the top 24 nations globally along with qualification slots for non-elite countries."
   },
   "12": {
    "original": "Jay Coates, Football Australia's Football Stakeholders Manager, accompanied by Member Federations President Luke Bessey watching the FIFA Council meeting in Moscow.",
    "rewrite": "Football Australia's Football Stakeholders Manager, Jay Coates, was joined by Member Federations President Luke Bessey as they observed the FIFA Council meeting in Moscow."
   },
   "1": {
    "original": "Participants will be divided into eight pots for the group stage draw, as opposed to the current format where the nations are separated according to region.",
    "rewrite": "Groups in the draw will be formed from eight pots, differing from the current system that divides nations by region."
   },
   "5": {
    "original": "But there are two other groups of nations lurking in pot one that will enjoy the fair draw during qualifying but lament the unfair draw at the finals.",
    "rewrite": "Yet, two additional groups of countries await their fate in pot one, relishing the fair distribution during qualifiers but later regretting what they see as an unfair treatment in the finals."
   },
   "6": {
    "original": "On a personal note, I don\u2019t have time to speak about the damage this will have on European teams and their fans.",
    "rewrite": "From a personal perspective, I do not have the time to discuss the impact this will have on European teams and their supporters."
   },
   "2": {
    "original": "These groups will be seeded too, with the top eight ranked teams placed in group A and so on down to group H.",
    "rewrite": "These teams will also be seeded, with the top eight ranked ones assigned to group A, progressing down to group H."
   },
   "8": {
    "original": "But it may be worth noting what various European journalists said at the time of the vote.",
